  "Id": 1383,
  "Title": "AKU Convocation 2011: Tanzania",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "Education and nursing graduates were honoured at a ceremony held at the Diamond Jubilee Hall in Dar es Salaam on February 9, 2011.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClassAB3722822E324A60A48F0EEA221ABD41\"><p>Education and nursing graduates were honoured at a ceremony held at the Diamond Jubilee Hall in Dar es Salaam on February 9, 2011.<br><br>The Aga Khan University Tanzania Institute of Higher Education awarded 28 students a Master of Education, 47 a Bachelor of Science in Nursing and 57 students were conferred a Diploma in General Nursing.<br><br>An award of academic excellence was presented to Prudensiana Cleophas Amlima who graduated with a Bachelor of Science degree in Nursing and Priciline Isack Mushi who graduated with a diploma in General Nursing. This award was presented to them for having demonstrated outstanding performance in their studies.<br><br>H.E Ali Hassan Mwinyi, Retired President of the United Republic of Tanzania was the Chief Guest.</p></div>",
